            "type": "verse",
            "performer": "",
            "lines": [
                {
                    "n": "0",
                    "text": "Sometimes a certain smell will take me back to when I was young",
                    "persona_id": "Clancy"
                },
                {
                    "n": "1",
                    "text": "How come I'm never able to identify where it's coming from?",
                    "persona_id": "Clancy"
                },
                {
                    "n": "2",
                    "text": "I'd make a candle out of it, if I ever found it",
                    "persona_id": "Clancy"
                },
                {
                    "n": "3",
                    "text": "Try to sell it, never sell out of it, I'd probably only sell one",
                    "persona_id": "Clancy"
                },
                {
                    "n": "4",
                    "text": "It'd be to my brother, 'cause we have the same nose",
                    "persona_id": "Clancy"
                },
                {
                    "n": "5",
                    "text": "Same clothes, homegrown, a stone's throw from a creek we used to roam",
                    "persona_id": "Clancy"
                },
                {
                    "n": "6",
                    "text": "But it would remind us of when nothing really mattered",
                    "persona_id": "Clancy"
                },
                {
                    "n": "7",
                    "text": "Out of student loans and treehouse homes, we all would take the latter",
                    "persona_id": "Clancy"
                }
            ]
